cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "photodyn2p: a TTV and photodynamical model for two planets, with a graphical user interface"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Vanaverbeke
    given-names: Siegfried
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0231-2676"
    affiliation: "Vereniging Voor Sterrenkunde, Mol, Belgium; Centre for Mathematical Plasma Astrophysics, KU Leuven, Belgium; Astrolab IRIS, Ypres, Belgium"
version: "1.1"
date-released: "2026-11-03"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23921757"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/svaverbe/photodyn2p"
url: "https://svaverbe.github.io/photodyn2p/"
abstract: >-
  photodyn2p models two gravitationally interacting planets around one star with the N-body code TTVFast.
  It fits mid-transit times, radial velocities and light curves (with a Gaussian process for stellar
  activity), using a global search (differential evolution), a maximum-likelihood fit and MCMC (emcee),
  and comes with a graphical user interface, a user manual and test examples with a known truth.
keywords:
  - exoplanets
  - transit timing variations
  - photodynamical modelling
  - N-body
  - MCMC
references:
  - type: article
    title: "TOI-3686: A Hot Jupiter and Sub-Neptune In A 2:1 Mean-Motion Resonance"
